            "review_title": "Review at Lily's Baradise and Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Susan M\nVung Tau, Vietnam13 contributions\n0\nSuse\nMar 2020 • Friends\nGreat pasta. If you want an oversized meal then maybe try somewhere they provide packet pasta.\nLily's bolognaise is authentic, first bite I knew it was hand made, waitress verified: 'daily on the premises.' Perfectly sized perfectly cooked strands. A small scoop of chocolate ice cream with wafer for desert was delicious. \nThe restraunt is going through a re-ferb and for my taste I'd say it's doing well. Service is friendly. A preferred 'go-to' for many of my friends who like to eat out in a casual holiday setting.\nBonus highlight: a patron handed out roses wishing us older girls 'happy international women's day'.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 8, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
